---
const FLOWCHART = `flowchart TD
    A["Rev-B submitted<br/>2026-05-14"]

    A --> B["1. Rev-C optics overhaul<br/>(recommended)"]
    A --> C["2. Firmware retry<br/>on Rev-B"]
    A --> D["3. Clinical pilot<br/>with §17 caveat"]
    A --> E["4. Hand over to<br/>next student"]

    B --> B1["Cross-position bench<br/>at GHE Lab"]
    B1 --> Field["Field deployment<br/>at a health centre"]

    C --> C1{"Closes §17<br/>±5% cross-position?"}
    C1 -->|likely no| B
    C1 -->|if yes| Field

    D --> D1["Document fixed-mount<br/>operating envelope"]
    D1 --> D2["Clinician feedback"]
    D2 --> B

    E --> E1["HANDOVER.md +<br/>this repository"]
    E1 --> E2["Continuation MSc / BSc<br/>at GHE or partner group"]
    E2 --> B

    classDef root fill:#1a4d8f,stroke:#0d2540,color:#ffffff,font-weight:bold
    classDef branch fill:#2d6a4f,stroke:#1b4332,color:#ffffff
    classDef decision fill:#f4a261,stroke:#e76f51,color:#2d2d2d
    classDef terminal fill:#9b2226,stroke:#660708,color:#ffffff,font-weight:bold
    classDef relay fill:#577590,stroke:#2c4356,color:#ffffff

    class A root
    class C1 decision
    class B,C,D,E branch
    class B1,D1,D2,E1,E2 relay
    class Field terminal
`;

const scenarios = [
  {
    tag: 'Hardware',
    title: '1. Rev-C optics overhaul',
    body: 'Add a second beam pair horizontally offset (to catch drop oscillation phase), widen TOP-BOT separation (to ensure drops fully detach before crossing TOP), and equalise TOP/BOT gain (to close the threshold-vs-peak baseline drift). Named in docs/limitations.md §§1, 3, 17 and HANDOVER.md. The recommended path — the position-dependence finding directly motivates these three changes, and the other three scenarios all eventually converge here.',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Firmware',
    title: '2. Smoothed-ADC peak detection retry',
    body: 'A few-hour experiment on existing Rev-B hardware. Median-of-N peak filter + open-loop core threshold derived from a fixed observed-peak constant rather than EMA. Probably blocked by §17 (threshold-vs-peak is at most one of three contaminants; umbilical and backsplash remain), but worth confirming before committing to silicon spin.',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Clinical',
    title: '3. Pilot with Rev-B at fixed mount',
    body: 'Deploy Rev-B at one health centre with the position constraint documented in the operating instructions (clamp the casing rigidly at a fixed height; recalibrate per session). Harvest clinician feedback on alarm patterns, mounting ergonomics, and battery life — the inputs Rev-C silicon design will need anyway.',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Succession',
    title: '4. Hand to a continuation thesis',
    body: 'HANDOVER.md + this repository + docs/decisions/* are the brief. A continuation MSc or BSc thesis takes the Rev-C optics path, the multi-board / multi-drip-set / multi-head-height generalisation runs that Rev-B left undone, or both. Pre-Delft exchange (autumn 2026) is the natural break-point on the current author\'s end.',
  },
];
---

<section id="future-work">
  <div class="eyebrow">Where do we go from here</div>
  <h2>Four paths out of Rev-B.</h2>
  <p class="lead">
    Rev-B's position-dependence finding (<a href="#limitations">§17</a>)
    points the architecture toward a Rev-C optics overhaul, but that's
    not the only response. Three lighter-touch paths converge to the
    same destination — clinical deployment of a position-invariant
    device — via different routes.
  </p>

  <div class="flowchart-wrap">
    <pre class="mermaid">{FLOWCHART}</pre>
  </div>

  <div class="scenarios-grid">
    {scenarios.map((s) => (
      <div class="scenario">
        <span class={`scen-tag scen-tag-${s.tag.toLowerCase()}`}>{s.tag}</span>
        <h3>{s.title}</h3>
        <p>{s.body}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
</section>

<script type="module" is:inline>
  import mermaid from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@10/dist/mermaid.esm.min.mjs';
  mermaid.initialize({
    startOnLoad: true,
    theme: 'default',
    securityLevel: 'loose',
    flowchart: { curve: 'basis', useMaxWidth: true, htmlLabels: true },
    themeVariables: {
      fontFamily: 'Inter, -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif',
      fontSize: '13px',
    },
  });
</script>

<style>
  #future-work {
    padding-top: 56px;
    padding-bottom: 56px;
  }
  #future-work h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 40px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    max-width: 22ch;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
  }
  #future-work a {
    color: var(--ir);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  #future-work a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .flowchart-wrap {
    background: #ffffff;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    padding: 28px 20px;
    margin: 36px 0 40px;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  pre.mermaid {
    margin: 0;
    text-align: center;
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: #2d2d2d;
  }

  .scenarios-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 18px;
  }
  .scenario {
    padding: 22px;
    background: var(--bg-2);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  .scenario h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.25;
    margin: 8px 0 10px;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .scenario p {
    color: var(--fg-dim);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .scen-tag {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    padding: 3px 8px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--fg-mute);
  }
  .scen-tag-hardware   { color: var(--ir);   border-color: var(--ir); }
  .scen-tag-firmware   { color: var(--flow); border-color: var(--flow); }
  .scen-tag-clinical   { color: #f4a261;     border-color: #f4a261; }
  .scen-tag-succession { color: #577590;     border-color: #577590; }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .scenarios-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    #future-work h2 { font-size: 30px; }
    .flowchart-wrap { padding: 14px 8px; }
    pre.mermaid { font-size: 11px; }
  }
</style>
